  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is making a layered cake consisting of 222 layers.\n\nChef has NNN options for the first layer, represented by an array A=[A1,A2,…,AN]A = [A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N]A=[A1​,A2​,…,AN​], where AiA_iAi​ represents the size of the iii-th first layer of the cake.\n\nSimilarly, Chef has MMM options for the second layer, represented by an array B=[B1,B2,…,BM]B = [B_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_M]B=[B1​,B2​,…,BM​], where BiB_iBi​ represents the size of the iii-th second layer of the cake.\n\nChef must ensure that the size of the second layer is **strictly smaller** than the size of the first layer. How many possible cakes can make by combining one first layer and one second layer, while respecting that constraint?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains 222 integers - NNN and MMM.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN integers - B1,B2,…,BMB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_MB1​,B2​,…,BM​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of valid layered cakes Chef can make.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N,M≤1001 \\le N, M \\le 1001≤N,M≤100",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤1001 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 1001≤Ai​,Bi​≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n4 2\n5 2 6 1\n3 7\n3 3\n3 3 3\n2 2 2\n1 1\n5\n2\n1 1\n1\n1",
        "output": "2\n9\n1\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : The 222 options are:\n\nChoosing A1=5A_1 = 5A1​=5 and B1=3B_1 = 3B1​=3.\nChoosing A3=6A_3 = 6A3​=6 and B1=3B_1 = 3B1​=3.\n\nTest Case 2 : Any of the first layer can be paired with any of the second layers. Thus, there are 3⋅3=93 \\cdot 3 = 93⋅3=9 pairs."
      }
    ]
